    "correction": "Czech has zero annotated damage boxes. Official evaluator zero placeholders do not mean zero detection ability; reviewed AP/recall/F1 are null. Historical notebook outputs and raw result JSON are retained unchanged.",
    "selection_limitation": "The training sample was enriched for damage. Its remaining same-country complement is depleted of positives: Japan supports only D00/D20; India has 42 boxes; Czech has zero boxes. These are selected-complement diagnostics, not representative country performance. No resampling after viewing scores.",
    "main_finding": "At frozen confidence 0.46 US pothole recall is 43/135 = 31.85% (92 missed); China development pothole recall is 227/235 = 96.60%. Do not tune on the now-inspected US set or claim this proves local robustness.",
    "visual_review": "Manually reviewed the original US and Czech galleries. US examples show unmatched small/fragmented labels and large predicted crack boxes spanning several labels. This is consistent with localization/label-granularity errors in those examples, not a verified population-level cause. Several Czech predictions overlap possible road joints/cracks despite empty labels, so they need annotation review; do not call all of them proven model false alarms or all empty-label images healthy roads.",
    "adoption": "Keep run17_best_finetuned.pt and confidence 0.46 as the frozen project candidate; cross-country failure remains unresolved. Local evaluation must report performance honestly. Any future tuning needs separate development data and a new untouched test set."
  }
